Package: gghalftone
Title: Halftone, Dither and Line-Screen Fills for 'ggplot2'
Version: 0.1.0
Date: 2026-09-29
Authors@R: person("Kinan", "El Husseini", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "kinelhu@gmail.com",
                  comment = c(ORCID = "0000-0001-9188-833X"))
Description: Halftone screens as ggplot2 layers. Dots are placed at draw time on a lattice with a physical pitch in
    millimetres, so a figure gets the same screen at any output size. Provides geom_halftone() for gridded fields,
    geom_spot() for per-point tone discs, with_halftone() to screen the fill of any layer (ribbons, areas, bars,
    polygons, sf), with_halo() and with_relief() for lines over a screen, a screen aesthetic for colour-free
    encodings, line screens, Bayer, blue-noise and Floyd-Steinberg dithering, overprinting of overlapping groups,
    with_press() for press artefacts, and a theme modifier with export helpers.
URL: https://github.com/kinelhu/gghalftone, https://kinelhu.github.io/gghalftone/
BugReports: https://github.com/kinelhu/gghalftone/issues
